.SH REQUIREMENTS
.\"
* Packages sapstartsrv-resource-agents TODO and resource-agents TODO, or newer.
.PP
* OS, Linux cluster and SAP instances are matching requirements for both, the
Filesystem resource based setup and the simple-mount setup.
.PP
* The resource configuration matches a documented setup. Even if the general
upgrade procedure is expected to work for customised configuration, details might
need special treatment.
.PP
* The SAP instance directories (/usr/sap/$SID/$InstanceName/) are provided on NFS
shares. If the instance directories are backed by local disks, additional steps
and services downtime are needed. This is out of scope for the procedure at hand.
.PP
* The whole upgrade procedure is tested carefully and documented in detail before
being applied on production.
.PP
* Linux cluster, SAP instances and enqueue replication are in sane state before
the upgrade. All cluster nodes are online. 
.PP
* The SAP instances are idle during the upgrade. No other changes on OS, cluster,
SAP instances or infrastructure are done in parallel to the upgrade.
.PP
* Password-less login for user root between cluster nodes. An upgrade is possible
without, but would need adapted commands. 
.PP
* Only one SAP system (SID) per cluster. An upgrade is possible with multiple SIDs,
but would need adapted commands.
.PP
* Two nodes per cluster. An upgrade is possible with three nodes, but would need
additional commands.
.PP
* Linux cluster, SAP instances and enqueueu replication are checked and in sane
state before set back into production.
.PP
